  "id": "DrugBank_DB08864 - MONDO_5109",
  "verbalization": "Rilpivirine is associated with the treatment of HIV infectious disease through a chain of indications that ultimately lead to this condition. The drug is indicated for AIDS, which in turn is linked to HIV infectious disease, and both AIDS and HIV infectious disease are indicated for other drugs such as elvitegravir, zalcitabine, and tenofovir disoproxil. These drugs are commonly used in the management of HIV, suggesting a shared therapeutic pathway. The evidence suggests that Rilpivirine may be repurposed for HIV infectious disease through its role in treating AIDS, which is a key step in the progression of HIV infection. The integration of these indications highlights the importance of Rilpivirine in the broader context of HIV treatment, emphasizing its potential role in the management of HIV infectious disease.",
